# STORYBOARD — Send to HyperFrames launch film

~50s @ 1920×1080, paper-launch aesthetic. Current = LEFT. Music-driven.
Every scene names its sustained-motion route (no dead time). Ledger.json before build.

---

## S1 — The invocation (0–12s) · route: cursor-led action → morph chain

Jake's choreography (2026-08-05). Bare paper throughout — no window chrome yet.

1. **S1a (0–2.5s)** — the Claude Design logo BUTTON, big and centered (spark +
   wordmark pill). Oversized macOS cursor enters off-screen, walks to it, CLICKS.
2. **S1b (2.5–6s)** — the click MORPHS the button into the prompt box (shared-element
   morph, Tier-A hand-authored: the hover pill grows into the white card while the
   "Design" letters dissolve — per ref video assets/ref/f02→f04→f07). Prompt types in.
   THE REF'S SIGNATURE MOVE: the background live-reacts to the typed prompt — at
   "dark navy" the paper world dips to navy; a ghost 2.4M numeral forms behind the box.
   Button/box anatomy is fixed by the ref: palette icon + "Design" (geometric sans),
   white card w/ gear/paperclip/pencil buttons + Import pill + coral paper-plane Send.
   Cursor is the WHITE macOS arrow (black outline) throughout the film.
3. **S1c (6–8.5s)** — prompt box SLIDES UP (nudge curve), revealing the workflow
   option cards beneath (waterfall entry). Cursor clicks **Animation**.
4. **S1d (8.5–11.5s)** — cursor clicks send → cut to BARE agent response on paper:
   serif streaming text ("Building it now — five scenes over ten seconds…"), caret
   blinking. No UI. Stillness (~0.4s) as the sentence completes.

- Seam S1d→S2: **cut-the-curve LEFT into the full UI view** — the response text exits
  left mid-motion; the full canvas editor enters left mid-flight.

## S2 — The playback + the send (12–24s) · route: camera with intent → cursor-led action

Jake's choreography (2026-08-06). The MERIDIAN VIDEO IS SQUARE (1080×1080) so it
formats cleanly at full-frame. Agent says "Done." (S1d, no caret) → cut-the-curve into:

1. **S2a** — full Claude Design UI, square Meridian video PLAYING in the canvas player
   (rail shows just "Done.").
2. **S2b** — at ~50% playback the video MORPHS to fill the whole frame (scale morph,
   carrier = the video frame itself; UI chrome falls away). Only a whisper-thin
   progress line survives at the bottom edge.
3. **S2c** — playback ends ON the full-frame final frame (MERIDIAN wordmark). The
   chrome REVEALS OVER the video: top scrim, Design/Code tabs, Share ▾. Cursor comes
   up, clicks Share → menu (Export: HTML/Canva/PDF/PowerPoint · Connectors: **Send to
   HyperFrames**) → CLICK. All of this happens with the video still full screen.
4. **S2d** — the video dims; the import card (tool call ✓ + square thumb + "Open in
   HyperFrames →") lands centered over it. That card is the CARRIER for the next seam.

- Seam S2→S3: Z-PULL (inverse zoom, camera back). The card/video plane shrinks mid-motion…

## S3 — The many (16–23s) · route: camera with intent + staged reveals

…and docks into a WALL of sessions — the ref's 28–29s look (assets/ref/g03.png,
g07.png): FULL Claude Design app windows (title tab + Project | name, Share + black
Export pill, Tweaks/Comment/Edit text/Knobs/Draw toolbar, chat rail with green-check
plan items struck through, dotted canvas), straight-tiled masonry with big cream
gutters, NO rotation, rows CROPPED at the frame edges so the wall reads as extending
beyond frame. Slow camera drift LEFT across the wall; 2–3 canvases visibly play.
Edge-cropped windows face their CANVAS toward frame center (rail gets cropped, not
content). Meridian sits center with its coral "Sent ✓" badge.

- Session variety (per ref): night-sky phone app, CRM dashboard, 3D house scene,
  globe hero, lava-lamp notification, DNA helix, egg phone, editorial quote.
- Seam S3→S4: Z-PUSH into a second window (camera forward, sign matched — window grows
  past frame edge as we enter it). Direction change is caused by a cursor click on that
  window (force spent).

## S4 — Again (23–29s) · route: cursor-led action (compressed reprise)

Inside project B's chat. Faster this time — the pattern is known: preview already built,
cursor goes straight to **Send to HyperFrames**, click, tool call, widget. Half S2's
duration; the film teaches by repetition, not narration.

- Seam S4→S5: UPWARD (reserved vector — elevation into the thesis). The widget card
  exits up mid-motion; the text beat's first word enters from below mid-flight.

## S5 — The thesis (29–35s) · text beat (mega-scale, ONE beat)

Paper goes full-bleed. Serif, ink on cream, waterfall entry word-by-word:

    **Claude designs it. HyperFrames completes it.**   (wording TBD — keep "completes")

"completes" lands last, in coral. THIS is where the music blooms from sparse to full —
the audio enacts "completes."

- Seam S5→S6: LEFT (back on the current). Text exits left mid-motion; the HyperFrames
  editor card enters left mid-flight.

## S6 — The completion (35–44s) · route: sequenced UI life

UI is the REAL hyperframes.dev/mcp-sessions editor (captured live from Jake's session,
2026-08-06; tokens in design-pass/k12.html): #0A0A0A ground, TT Norms Pro, three panes —
Tasks rail | player + scene-block timeline (INSIDE: MAIN, s1…sN, green playhead) |
Chat/Renders panel with green status dots ("Preview updated"), REAL suggestion chips
("Add an energetic soundtrack" / "Add sound effects on the key moments" / "Add a whoosh
as the title appears" / "Punch up the motion and tighten the pacing"), "Send a message"
composer with green send. Top bar: green Export, Publish/Download/Private pills, Draft.
Agent avatar = ORB.svg. Claude cameo stays coral; HyperFrames world is green.

Faithful HyperFrames mcp-session editor. First-run enhance suggestion chips visible
("Add sound", "Polish the motion" — Somansh's real chips). Cursor taps one; the enhance
agent responds; a progress state; then the agent turn: **"Your video is ready."** with
the rendered player.

- Stillness-before-climax: 0.5s hold on "ready" before the play click.

## S7 — The output (44–52s) · the recursive payoff

Cursor clicks play → the rendered video goes FULL-FRAME (carrier: the player expands
through the seam, Z-push). And the video the agent made is… a launch spot for the
connection itself: project B WAS "a video about sending Claude designs to HyperFrames."
It ends on the CTA card, now with sound and polish the Claude draft never had:

    Claude Design → **Send to HyperFrames**
    Try the connection.

Hold, grain breathing at grade level only. End.

